# build outputs: the Windows bats put .obj in SRC/out/<arch> (out/x86, out/x64) -
# one dir per arch, so both builds coexist and each carries its own SDL2.dll; SRC/.gitignore
# has the out/ rule itself. CMake gets one dir per flavour: build-win32/, build-win64/
# on Windows, build/ (or build32/, build64/) on Linux, build-switch/ for the .nro. One dir
# per flavour matters because SDL2/libavcodec must come from the matching
# architecture, so a dir is tied to one of them for good.
*.obj
*.exe
*.pdb
*.map
*.ilk
*.dll
*_debug.log
build_dbg*.log
build*/

# third_party SDKs are committed as-is (SDL2.dll must not be ignored)
!third_party/**

# original game data and saves - never commit
*.SAV
*.avi
*.AVI
FINAL.BMP
INTRO.BMP
START.BMP
PILOTS.iso
PILOTS0
PILOTS0.*

# the exe's icon is carved out of PILOTS.EXE by scripts/extract_icon.ps1, so it
# is original game data just like the source file and must not be committed.
# The bats regenerate it on demand; *.res is its compiled intermediate.
SRC/pilots.ico
*.res
